                <section class="content-section" id="what-is-secops">
                    <h2>What is SecOps?</h2>
                    <p>
                        <strong>ServiceNow Security Operations (SecOps)</strong> is a platform that bridges the gap 
                        between IT security teams and IT operations by orchestrating and automating incident and 
                        vulnerability management workflows.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        SecOps does <strong>not replace</strong> your existing security tools (SIEM, vulnerability 
                        scanners, EDR, firewalls). Instead, it acts as a central <strong>orchestration layer</strong> 
                        that ingests data from these disparate tools, enriches it with business context from the 
                        CMDB, and triggers automated, prioritized workflows.
                    </p>
                    <div class="info-card info-card--important">
                        <div class="info-card-title">Key Mental Model</div>
                        <p>
                            Think of SecOps as the "air traffic control" for your security ecosystem. Your SIEM 
                            detects threats, your scanners find vulnerabilities, your EDR monitors endpoints — 
                            SecOps coordinates the response across all of them and connects it to the business 
                            context of what's actually at risk.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section class="content-section" id="soar">
                    <h2>SOAR Capabilities</h2>
                    <p>
                        SecOps functions as a full <strong>SOAR (Security Orchestration, Automation, and Response)</strong> 
                        platform with three pillars:
                    </p>

                    <div class="tabs-container">
                        <div class="tabs-header">
                            <button class="tab-btn active" data-tab="tab-orchestration">Orchestration</button>
                            <button class="tab-btn" data-tab="tab-automation">Automation</button>
                            <button class="tab-btn" data-tab="tab-response">Response</button>
                        </div>
                        <div class="tab-panel active" id="tab-orchestration">
                            <h3>Security Orchestration</h3>
                            <p>
                                Connects your entire security ecosystem into a single pane of glass. SIEM alerts, 
                                vulnerability scan results, EDR detections, and threat intelligence feeds all flow 
                                into SecOps, correlated against your CMDB.
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Pre-built connectors</strong> for Splunk, QRadar, CrowdStrike, Qualys, Tenable, and 50+ tools</li>
                                <li><strong>IntegrationHub</strong> for custom REST-based integrations</li>
                                <li><strong>Bidirectional sync</strong> — actions taken in SecOps can be pushed back to source tools</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-automation">
                            <h3>Security Automation</h3>
                            <p>
                                Replaces manual, repetitive tasks with automated playbooks. This reduces Mean Time 
                                to Respond (MTTR) and frees analysts for higher-value work.
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Alert triage:</strong> Auto-prioritize based on CMDB business criticality</li>
                                <li><strong>Data enrichment:</strong> Auto-query VirusTotal, WHOIS, passive DNS for observables</li>
                                <li><strong>Containment actions:</strong> Auto-isolate hosts, block IPs, disable accounts</li>
                                <li><strong>Notification routing:</strong> Auto-notify stakeholders based on affected services</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-response">
                            <h3>Security Response</h3>
                            <p>
                                Structured, auditable response workflows with full accountability. Every action 
                                is logged, every decision is traceable, and every response follows organizational policy.
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Playbook-driven:</strong> Guided task sequences for different incident types</li>
                                <li><strong>Multi-team collaboration:</strong> Security, IT, legal, and PR working in one record</li>
                                <li><strong>SLA tracking:</strong> Built-in SLA management for response time commitments</li>
                                <li><strong>Post-incident review:</strong> Structured PIR with knowledge article generation</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

